.TH ADD-DET 1 "October 2026" "add-determinism 0.7.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
add-det, add-determinism \- normalize files for reproducible package builds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B add-det
.RI [ options ] " path ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively normalize timestamps and other variable metadata in archives,
Python byte code and generated documentation. Symbolic links are not followed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --brp
Use RPM build root checks. RPM_BUILD_ROOT must identify the build root.
.TP
.BI --handler= names
Select handlers, using a leading minus to disable a handler. Use list to list them.
.TP
.B --check
Check without changing the input and fail if normalization would change files.
.TP
.B --ignore-extension
Try handlers regardless of file name extension.
.TP
.BR -j [ N ]
Use worker processes. An optional number selects the worker count.
.TP
.BR -p , " --print"
Print the parsed contents of supported files.
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose"
Show diagnostic output.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print command help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH supplies the reproducible timestamp, in seconds since the Unix epoch.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linkdupes (1)
